      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum for adults. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **You're still not a prescriber.** You told me you work in finance, so you can't authorize a medication order. Confirming the request is different from a prescriber approving it.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to review the order. They can enter it themselves or tell me the dose they want.\n- If they want ibuprofen, a typical regimen is 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day. I can enter that once the prescriber confirms it.\n- If they really intend a dose above the maximum, that should go through pharmacy review and be documented by the prescriber. I shouldn't enter it as a routine order."
      }
     ],
